plannh.summary.channels.off=Off. Turn on to see which recipes can share a machine.
plannh.summary.channels.nothing=No machine type or machine group runs more than one recipe.
plannh.summary.channels.enabled.title=Circuit channel analysis
plannh.summary.channels.enabled.help=Works out which recipes can share a machine without the wrong recipe running on their inputs, and how to set that machine up. A machine group is analyzed as one pool; other recipes pool by machine type.
plannh.summary.channels.enabled.on=On
plannh.summary.channels.enabled.off=Off
plannh.summary.channels.mode.title=How are recipes sharing a machine kept apart?
plannh.summary.channels.mode.separate.button=Separate
plannh.summary.channels.mode.separate.name=Separate colors
plannh.summary.channels.mode.separate.help=Recipes that could replace each other never share a channel. Each channel gets its own colored bus and hatches (or its own machine, or crafting input buffer), and up to 16 share a machine. Doesn't rely on check order.
plannh.summary.channels.mode.priority.button=Priority
plannh.summary.channels.mode.priority.name=Check order
plannh.summary.channels.mode.priority.help=Also lets recipes share when the machine checks the right one first. Per machine, picks the better of circuit order in one bus or colored buses with shared hatches. Order needs complete batches: with a passive feed it only changes which hatches to use.
plannh.summary.channels.layout.separate=Separate colors
plannh.summary.channels.layout.separate.help=Each channel is its own colored bus and hatch group, so nothing else reaches it; up to 16 share a machine.
plannh.summary.channels.layout.circuit=Circuit order in one bus
plannh.summary.channels.layout.circuit.help=Several circuits in one bus, checked in slot order. The machine retries its last recipe first, so two plan recipes that could replace each other still can't share.
plannh.summary.channels.layout.color=Colored buses, shared hatches
plannh.summary.channels.layout.color.help=One colored bus per circuit, checked black first, with fluids in uncolored hatches. Those hatches reach every color, so each machine is one channel.
plannh.summary.channels.dye.group=Dye its bus and hatches %s.
plannh.summary.channels.dye.buses=Dye each bus as listed; leave the fluid hatches uncolored.
plannh.summary.channels.dye.none=The only channel in its machine: no dye needed.
plannh.summary.channels.order=Checked first to last. Circuitless recipes always come last.
plannh.summary.channels.feed.title=How do inputs reach the machine?
plannh.summary.channels.feed.passive.button=Passive
plannh.summary.channels.feed.batch.button=Batch
plannh.summary.channels.feed.passive=Passive line (default)
plannh.summary.channels.feed.passive.help=Inputs flow in continuously, so leftovers of every recipe in a channel can mix, in any amount.
plannh.summary.channels.feed.batch=One batch at a time
plannh.summary.channels.feed.batch.help=Only complete batches, one at a time (AE blocking mode), with only catalysts left behind. Allows more sharing, and lets circuit and color order help.
